test/check/error-bad-arguments.sumspec:6:52:
  |
6 | Page = Home | Plan Mode | Pick (One | Two) | Many [A]
  |                                                    ^
warning: a list goes only as a whole type definition; give it a type name, such as Points = [Point], and write the name here (an error from SumSpec 1.2)

test/check/error-bad-arguments.sumspec:9:10:
  |
9 | onSum :: Mode(Map) -> Mode
  |          ^
Mode is a sum; pick a variant with "." instead of arguments

test/check/error-bad-arguments.sumspec:10:13:
   |
10 | onAtomic :: A(B) -> A
   |             ^
A takes no arguments

test/check/error-bad-arguments.sumspec:10:13:
   |
10 | onAtomic :: A(B) -> A
   |             ^
warning: onAtomic changes one A of a list, but doesn't say which; to pick it, compare a key with a named value, such as A(id * ...)

test/check/error-bad-arguments.sumspec:11:21:
   |
11 | onNoPayload :: Page.Home(A) -> Page.Home
   |                     ^
Page.Home takes no arguments

test/check/error-bad-arguments.sumspec:12:17:
   |
12 | tooMany :: Page.Plan(Mode.Map * Mode.Plot) -> Page.Home
   |                 ^
Page.Plan takes one argument, Mode, but 2 are given

test/check/error-bad-arguments.sumspec:13:24:
   |
13 | wrongType :: Page.Plan(A) -> Page.Home
   |                        ^
expected Mode here, not A

test/check/error-bad-arguments.sumspec:14:25:
   |
14 | wrongList :: Page.Many([B]) -> Page.Pick(One)
   |                         ^
expected [A] here, not [B]

test/check/error-bad-arguments.sumspec:14:25:
   |
14 | wrongList :: Page.Many([B]) -> Page.Pick(One)
   |                         ^
warning: a list isn't written in a pattern; give it a type name, such as Ids = [Id], and write the name (Ids, or Ids#ids to name it) (an error from SumSpec 1.2)

test/check/error-bad-arguments.sumspec:14:37:
   |
14 | wrongList :: Page.Many([B]) -> Page.Pick(One)
   |                                     ^
Page.Pick is a sum; pick a variant with "." instead of arguments

